          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Brachythecium salebrosum is a species of moss in the Brachytheciaceae family. It is widely distributed throughout the world, except for in South-America and in tropical regions."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Brachythecium salebrosum is known to be able to use artificial light to grow in places which are otherwise devoid of natural light, such as Crystal Cave in Wisconsin."
          }
        ]
